Abrahoma Bentaal.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''Abrahoma Bentaal''' was the [[Planetary Governor|governor]] of the [[Penal World]] of [[Kernak V]] in the [[Age of the Dark Imperium]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
When [[Inquisitor]] [[Sahansun]] proposed the creation of [[Cordon Impenetra|a fortified area of space]] to protect the wider [[Imperium]] from potential spillover from the ongoing [[Octarius War]], Governor Bentaal was one of the Imperial Commanders he contacted. Bentaal readily accepted the inclusion of Kernak V into the defence network.{{Fn|1}}

Sure enough, the [[ork]]s did end up moving on the [[Kernak System]]. An army of greenskins led by the notorious [[Nabrot Stubfingers]] quickly rolled over and crushed the defenders of [[Kernak III]] and [[Kernak IV|IV]]. However, they had a much harder time when they attacked Kernak V, as Governor Bentaal (having heard of large scale riots occurring on other Imperial Penal Worlds) had made sure her world had a sizeable and well-equipped garrison of troops.{{Fn|1}}

Despite the successes of the Imperial garrison, Stubfingers' [[Boyz]] were eventually reinforced by a fleet led by [[Stugbrog|Stugbrog da Facegrinda]]. Stugbrog's massed armoured assault overwhelmed Kernak V's defenders and even after the bulk of da Facegrinda's forces left in search of a new scrap elsewhere, the remnants were still too numerous to defeat. Bentaal reluctantly ordered the evacuation of the remaining Imperial troops, which were sent to [[Kernak II]] or the worlds of the [[Suvardosha System]], and left Kernak V's prisoners to die. Although it is the Governor's hope that Imperial forces can be consolidated and remarshaled to liberate Kernak V in future.{{Fn|1}}

