Acronis.wikitext:
{{RavenGuardPortal}}
'''Acronis''' was a member of the [[Raven Guard]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]] and the commander of the [[Ad Temperesta]]. He took part in the [[Great Crusade]] and the [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1a}}
==History==
He was born on [[Shale Gamma]] and was forced to survive on his own within its dangerous '''Rust Spoils'''. This harsh existence continued, until Acronis was recruited by the [[Raven Guard]] and for the first time in his life, he was no longer alone. There were now others to help him and lead Acronis into the future the [[Imperium]] was creating. His experiences in the Rust Spoils, though, left an impression on Acronis and taught him that survival, watchfulness and lethality, were one and the same. It also caused Acronis to seek out solitude and this caused him to join the Raven Guard's recon units. There, he put the skills he honed on Shale Gamma, into use far behind enemy lines. Eventually, however, Acronis began commanding his [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]]'s reconnaissance ships and by the time of the [[Horus Heresy]], he had command of the [[Ad Temperesta]].{{Fn|1a}}

When the [[Raven Guard]]'s [[Primarch]], [[Corvus Corax]], received word that [[Warmaster]] [[Horus]] had [[Horus Heresy|rebelled]] against the [[Imperium]], he sought to confirm this was true. This led the Primarch to order the [[Ad Temperesta]] into the [[Isstvan System]] and the [[Symphalia Class Warp Runner]] found evidence that the [[Isstvan-III Atrocity]] had occurred. Its sensors then detected a residue trail of spaceship [[vox]] signals, which Acronis ordered the Ad Temperesta to follow. This led to the discovery, that Warmaster Horus and the [[Traitor Legions]] had built a base on [[Isstvan V]].{{Fn|1a}} All of this information was then relayed to the Imperium and plans were made for its forces to attack the world and end Horus' rebellion. When the time came for the invasion to occur, the Ad Temperesta created a navigational beacon that led to Isstvan V. Its [[Navigator]] then sent this out, as the Warp Runner entered the [[Warp]] and left the [[System]].{{Fn|1b}} 

The beacon was used by the [[Imperium]]'s forces to attack [[Isstvan V]],{{Fn|1b}} but this was a trap set by the [[Warmaster]] and the [[Dropsite Massacre]] began. The ambush led to the near destruction of the [[Raven Guard]], [[Iron Hands]] and [[Salamanders]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]]s and revealed that [[Horus]]' [[Horus Heresy|rebellion]] was much larger than the Imperium had thought. The [[Ad Temperesta]] was able to bear witness to all of this, as Acronis had ordered the [[Symphalia Class Warp Runner|Warp Runner]] to re-enter the [[Isstvan System]] and it reached the world just as the Massacre began. There was little he could do to aid the Imperium or the Raven Guard, however, as the Ad Temperesta was meant for stealth and not for battle. Instead, he had the Warp Runner's sensors take in everything, as he stood and watched the near death of his Legion.{{Fn|1c}} When the Massacre was over, Acronis sent everything the Ad Temperesta had learned to [[Terra]] and then continued to monitor the Traitor Legions. He also sought to search for [[Vox]] signals from any [[Imperial]] survivors. This led Acronis to remain in the [[System]], until the Warp Runner was at risk of being discovered.{{Fn|1d}}

==Sources==
