Aelos.wikitext:
{{GreyKnightsPortal}}
'''Aelos''' is a [[Grey Knights]] [[Justicar]], whose [[power armor]] is decorated with records of valor, earned during his long service to the [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1}} 
==History==
He was also once the mentor of [[Graucis Telomane]], who was once among the [[Justicar]]'s wards as they began their training to become [[Grey Knight]]s. Though the two had a close relationship, though a major disagreement occurred when the [[First War of Armageddon]] began. At that time, Telomane had just joined the ranks of its [[Grey Knights Brotherhood|Brotherhoods]], but had been asked by [[Grey Knights Captain|Captain]] [[Taremar Aurellian]] to take part in the [[Chapter]]'s targeted strike against the [[Daemon Primarch]] [[Angron]]. Aelos vehemently disagreed with this and refused to give Telomane permission to do so, as he claimed the young Grey Knight was not ready to face such a powerful foe. In the Justicar's words, there was a reason the Chapter did not temper its youngest members in battle. Telomane believed he was ready, however, and chose to ignore his mentor's warning and join the attack anyways. In the end, Telomane was among the thirteen Grey Knights who survived the battle, that saw Angron banished to the [[Warp]], but he was left severely wounded afterwards.{{Fn|1}}     

However, that meeting between them would be the last time that Aelos and [[Graucis Telomane|Telomane]] saw each other. In the hundreds of years since then, the young [[Grey Knight]] has become an experienced [[Epistolary]] with a high standing within their [[Chapter]]. But while Telomane has outgrown his former mentor in many ways, he still remembers Aelos as the colossus he viewed the [[Justicar]] as, during their last meeting together.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Angron: The Red Angel (Novel)]], Chapter 1  

