Aetian Keltos.wikitext:
{{SpaceMarinePortal}}
'''Aetian Keltos''' is a [[Primaris Lieutenant]] in the [[Silver Templars]]'s [[Space Marine Company|4th Company]], whose battles with the forces of [[Chaos]] have already entered the [[Chapter]]'s legends.{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
He was among the [[Mars|Martian]] [[Primaris Space Marines]] that were awoken at the start of the [[Indomitus Crusade]] and inducted into the newly created [[Silver Templars]]. As the Crusade began to reclaim the [[Imperium]]'s lost worlds, the Silver Templars joined [[Indomitus Crusade Fleet Primus]] and Keltos served as an [[Intercessor]] [[Space Marine Sergeant]] in [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Markos Lukion]]'s [[Space Marine Company|4th Company]]. Under his leadership, '''Squad Keltos''' soon earned a reputation as one of the 4th's most reliable squadrons and were renowned for killing enemy leaders and champions. Keltos slew several powerful foes in single combat during these battles and with each fight, he honed his skills as both a leader and a duellist.{{Fn|1}} 

Several years later, as the [[Indomitus Crusade]] waged on, the [[Space Marine Company|4th Company's]] losses began to mount and among them was [[Primaris Lieutenant|Lieutenant]] [[Gianos Raksis]]. The Lieutenant was slain in fierce combat with the [[Black Legion]] on [[Gentu III]] and afterwards [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Markos Lukion|Lukion]] immediately promoted Keltos to the rank of Lieutenant and he then led his Demi-Company to victory and drove the traitors from Gentu III. Eventually, the Silver Templars earned the right to claim [[Novaris]] as their [[Adeptus Astartes Homeworld|Homeworld]] and the bulk of the Chapter departed Fleet Primus for their new home.{{Fn|1}}

The 4th Company was among the Silver Templars who accompanied the Ultramarines as they defended [[Ultramar]], during the [[Plague Wars]]. There, the Company fought many battles against the [[Death Guard]] and the losses they suffered were replaced by the first wave of Silver Templars born on Novaris. These new Primaris Space Marines excelled under Keltos' command and he went on to lead his reinforced Demi-Company to several victories over the Death Guard.{{Fn|1}}

After years of further fighting, the [[Death Guard]] withdrew to the [[Scourge Stars]] and created a lull in the fighting within [[Ultramar]]. This allowed Keltos to visit his [[Adeptus Astartes Homeworld|Homeworld]] for the first time and he would immerse himself in its population's culture. This earned him praise from his [[Space Marine Company|Demi-Company]] and eased the remaining tensions between the Martian and Novarian Silver Templars. This was noticed by [[Chapter Master]] [[Akilios Zanaris]], who was impressed by Keltos' leadership skills and believed the [[Primaris Lieutenant|Lieutenant]] had the makings of a future [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]].{{Fn|1}}

Sometime later, Keltos' Demi-Company would begin waging war once again and took part in the battle for the [[Forest World]] [[Ultach]]. There they clashed with not only the [[Black Legion]], but also the [[Death Guard]] forces of the [[Daemon Prince]] [[Mytoxis]]. As the war on Ultach raged, Keltos led a strike team to hunt down the Daemon Prince and he intended to personally put an end to Mytoxis' schemes on the world.{{Fn|1}}

==Wargear==
Keltos is armed with the [[Master Crafted]] [[Power Sword]] [[Mercy]] and the [[Heavy Bolt Pistol]] [[Absolution]]. As with keeping with the [[Silver Templars]] traditions, each weapon was crafted by Keltos' hands.{{Fn|1}}

