Aettius Vasta.wikitext:
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
'''Aettius Vasta''' was an [[Ultramarines]] [[Praetor (Rank)|Consul-Praetor]], who took part in the [[Great Crusade]] and [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
He was stationed on the [[Ultramar]] world [[Armatura]], when it was attacked by the [[Horus Heresy|Heresy]]'s [[Shadow Crusade]]. As the [[World Eaters]] and [[Word Bearers]] invaded, Vasta led the [[Imperial]] defenses in the '''Decalian District'''. It was a key area that guarded the approaches to the [[Ultramarines]]' planetary headquarters on Armatura. They were then attacked by the World Eaters and were able to keep the traitors back. This changed, though, when the [[Traitor Legion]]'s [[Red Hand]] [[Destroyer Squad]]s entered the fray. Their deadly weaponry began to push the Imperials back and they soon suffered another blow. This occurred when the [[Legio Lysanda]] [[Titan]]s that had been aiding them, withdrew to combat the traitorous [[Legio Audax]] elsewhere.{{Fn|1}} 

The loss of the [[Titan]]s' support allowed the [[World Eaters]] to begin overwhelming Vasta's forces. To prevent their defeat, the [[Praetor (Rank)|Consul-Praetor]] ordered his [[Ultramarines]] to immediately entrench further into the '''Decalian District'''. In order to do so, however, the [[Highborn Wardens]] [[Solar Auxilia]] and the Legion's [[Evocati]] remained behind, so the bulk of the Ultramarines could withdraw. They succeeded, but Vasta's defense was ultimately ended, when [[Jump Pack]]-equipped [[Red Hand]] [[Destroyer Squad]]s, fired their weaponry on the Ultramarines' position. Though it killed their fellow World Eaters as well, the Red Hand's attack allowed the [[Traitor Legion]] to overrun the [[Imperial]]s. Vasta would be among the last to die and fell after his [[power armor]] had been hacked open in a dozen places.{{Fn|1}}

