Agamorr.wikitext:
{{DeathwatchPortal}}
[[Brother-Sergeant]] '''Agamorr''' is a member of the [[Deathwatch]] from the [[Hammers of Retribution]] [[Space Marine Chapter]].{{Fn|1a}}

==History==
Wielding his ancient [[thunder hammer]], Agamorr has served in the Deathwatch for just over three decades; his original standard ten-year tour of duty was extended when it was discovered that he had a knack for eliminating unusual xenoforms.{{Fn|1a}}

==Twilight==
{{spoiler|source=Dark Heresy: Purge the Unclean}}
[[File:Brother-SergeantAgamorr.png |right|thumb|250px|Agamorr{{Fn|1a}}]]
Agamorr assisted [[Inquisitor]] [[Vaarak]]'s  [[Acolyte]]s in boarding the [[Space Hulk]] ''[[Twilight]]'', after a distress signal identified as belonging to the legendary [[Daemonhunter]] [[Adorjin]], who was last seen boarding a [[League of Blackships|Blackship]] and had been missing for six centuries. The [[Inquisition]] felt honourbound to try to determine Adorjin’s fate and recover her legendary holy blade, the ''[[Luminous Reproach]]'', which had been blessed by [[Sebastian Thor]] himself and had a long history of service in the Inquisition.{{Fn|1b}}

The Acolytes and Agamorr had just over fifteen hours to determine what happened to Adorjin and flee the ''Twilight'', as [[Battlefleet Calixis]] would destroy the space hulk before it collided with the planet [[Scintilla]], the sector capital of the [[Calixis Sector]]. Entering the space hulk they encountered [[Warp Ghosts]] of the [[psykers]] slain aboard the missing Blackship and battled [[Dark Eldar]] and [[Warp Beasts]] from the [[Kabal of Crimson Woes]].{{Fn|1b}} It was after a battle with the Kabal that the mission turned against the group, as in a final act of defiance one of its dying members blew into the [[Omni-Dimensional Whistle]] and called forth a horde of warp beasts to overwhelm them. Thinking quickly, Agamorr pushed the acolytes out of the way and ordered them to continue the mission. Standing defiantly in front of the daemons, he held the warp beasts at bay long enough for them to get away before he was engulfed by the horde.{{Fn|1c}}

Heeding his orders, the Acolytes moved quickly and began to home in on Adorijin's signal. Entering the remnants of the Blackship, they encountered another group of acolytes sent by Inquisitor [[Soldevan]] of the [[Ordo Hereticus]]. After a tense standoff they agreed to work together.{{Fn|1d}} Advancing further into the Blackship, they found the remains of Inquisitor Adorjin and [[Nekaybraianon]], the [[Daemon Prince]] she slew. They retrieved the ''Luminous Reproach'' as well as the ''[[Liber Daemonica]]'', a book on denizens of the [[warp]].{{Fn|1e}} As the Acolytes made their way to the [[escape pod]]s within the Blackship they were attacked by the Crimson Woes in overwhelming numbers. Things turned even more desperate as [[Forden|one of Soldevan's acolytes]] grabbed the ''Liber Daemonica'' and revealed himself to be secretly working for the [[Serrated Query]], a group of war profiteers working with the Kabal.{{Fn|1f}}

Just as the acolytes were about to be killed, Agamorr entered the battle, killing several of the Crimson Woes in seconds. Though his armour was severely wrecked and he had suffered numerous wounds to his body, Agamorr was able to turn the tide of battle in the acolytes' favour. The group managed to kill the traitor acolyte and retrieve the ''Liber Daemonica''. Just then the space hulk began to tilt as Battlefleet Calixis began bombarding it. The surviving Crimson Woes retreated into the warp and the group made its way to the escape pods. Just after they were launched, the space hulk broke apart behind them.{{Fn|1f}}

