Agastus (Dreadnought).wikitext:
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
'''Agastus''' is a [[Brutalis Dreadnought]] in the [[Ultramarines]] [[Chapter]], who is the leader of [[Strike Force Agastus (Ultramarines)|Strike Force Agastus]].{{Fn|1a}}
==History==
Before his internment, Agastus was a [[Chaplain]] who served as a mentor to his fellow [[Ultramarine]] [[Lasandro Titus]] and they would become friends as well. This mentorship and friendship remained true, even after Agastus' was wounded and placed within a [[Brutalis Dreadnought]]. When Titus became a [[Primaris Lieutenant|Lieutenant]] and was given command of a strike force, he chose his mentor to be its true leader. This went against the [[Codex Astartes]], but none doubted Agastus was still a mighty force of the [[Emperor]]'s will and Titus' decision was allowed to remain. The Dreadnought has since led [[Strike Force Agastus (Ultramarines)|Strike Force Agastus]] to victories over the [[Imperium]]'s foes,{{Fn|1a}} such as on [[Idrapol]] where they defeated the [[Master-Mek]]'s [[Ork]] forces.{{Fn|1b}} The Strike Force is currently among the Imperial's forces defending the besieged [[Tarmoth System]], from a massive Ork [[Waaagh!]]. The [[Xenos]] have now invaded the [[Agri World]] [[Kolomar]] and Strike Force Agastus has been sent to repel the Orks. They have since been deployed from their [[Strike Cruiser]], [[Pride of Talassar]], and are utilizing hit and run tactics against the invading Orks.{{Fn|1a}}   

Before one such attack occurred, [[Lasandro Titus|Titus]] made banter with Agastus and mentioned their successful battle against the [[Master-Mek]]. At first, however his mentor did not remember the battle on [[Idrapol]], until Titus provided more details, which finally jogged Agastus' memory. Though the [[Brutalis Dreadnought]] tried to cover this lapse with humor, Titus became concerned and privately asked Agastus if he was up to leading the attack. While Agastus did admit he was not who he once was and was still getting used to being a Dreadnought, he was adamant that his ability to wage war should never be doubted. Titus quickly assured his mentor, that though he knew Agastus was suffering, the [[Primaris Lieutenant|Lieutenant]] would rather die than ever doubt his old friend. Agastus thanked him and then told the Strike Force to ready themselves and be prepared to retreat, when the order was given. The Orks attacked shortly afterwards and though the Strike Force killed many of them, [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] [[Kaldan]] squad learned that a second wave began to approach their location. By then, however, Agastus was lost to battle fevour and was engaged in heavy melee combat, so the Sergeant brought the information to Titus. Kaldan then suggested they call in their gunship to evacuate and the Lieutenant agreed. Titus ordered Kaldan to ready his squad and the wounded to be evacuated, while he took Sergeant [[Haspian]]'s squad to rally to Agastus' position. He could see that the Dreadnought risked being overwhelmed and they would need to perform a fighting retreat afterwards. As they raced towards his old mentor's side, Titus vowed that he would not let his friend be overcome.{{Fn|1b}}

==Sources==
*1: [[Strike Force Agastus]] ''Rules Booklet''
**{{Endn|1a}}: pgs. 2-4
**{{Endn|1b}}: pgs. 9-10

