Aiakos.wikitext:
{{SpaceMarinesPortal}}
[[Image:Hecaton.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Hecaton Aiakos]]
'''Aiakos''', the '''Guardian of the ''[[Daedelos Krata]]''''' and the '''Terror of [[Bifrost]]''', is a [[Contemptor Pattern Dreadnought]] '''Hecaton''' of the [[Minotaurs]] who has been in service with the [[Chapter]] for several centuries.{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
Aiakos has served at the forefront of a dozen major campaigns, including leading the boarding assault against the [[Lamenters]] [[Strike Cruiser]] ''Mater Suspiria'' during the [[Badab War|Battle of Optera]] and the defence of the Black Gates of Hive Vitria against the [[Genestealer Cult|Genestealer Cult of the Dreaming Deeps]].{{fn|1}}

Most infamously, Aiakos rampaged through allied lines during the [[Bifrost Uprising]] after he was mistakenly fired upon by a detachment of [[Bifrost Huscarls]] under the command of [[Brother-Sergeant]] [[Augustine]] of the [[Viper Legion]] Chapter. Enraged, Aiakos killed thirty-seven Huscarls and Augustine himself, ripping apart a [[Leman Russ Battle Tank]] that tried to stop him. His assault was only halted after he received an emergency countermand signal from the Minotaurs [[Chapter Master]] in orbit.{{Fn|1}}

During the [[Orphean War]], Aiakos was armed with a [[Dreadnought Close Combat Weapon#Power Fist|Dreadnought Power Fist]] and a [[Plasma Cannon]]. The shield generator mounted on his shoulder augments the Dreadnought's [[Atomantic Shielding]].{{Fn|1}}

==Trivia==
{{trivia}}
*[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aeacus Aeacus] is the son of Europa by Zeus (who abducted her in the form of a sacred bull) in Greek mythology, making him the half-brother of King Minos of Crete.

