Akanabekh.wikitext:
{{NecronPortal}}
'''Akanabekh''' is the current [[Phaeron]] of the [[Necron]] [[Kardenath Dynasty]].  He is also the Regent of the [[Tomb World]] of [[Nagathar]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
Like many in his [[Necron Dynasty|Dynasty]], Akanabekh seeks to destroy all life in the [[Galaxy]]. This led him to command [[Kardenath Dynasty|Kardenath]]'s forces, as they sought to claim the [[Oruscar Dynasty]]'s [[Celestial Orrery]], which resided on the [[Tomb World]] [[Thanatos]]. The powerful relic had the power to fulfill his Dynasty's wish, but they were kept at bay by Oruscar forces, who were led by the [[Conclave of Celestial Guardians]]. They were charged by their Dynasty with defending the Orrery and the resulting [[Siege of Thanatos|siege]] between Kardenath and Oruscar has lasted for centuries.{{Fn|2}} 

In late [[M41]], however, the [[Phaeron]] was approached by [[Trazyn the Infinite]], who wished to form an alliance in order to bring the conflict to an end. In return for Akanabekh ordering his forces to make a frenzied attack on the walls defending the Orrery, Trazyn would sneak into the [[Conclave of Celestial Guardians|Conclave]]'s chambers with the Phaeron hidden within a [[Tesseract Labyrinth]]. The [[Necron Overlord|Overlord]] would then unleash Akanabekh, so that he could finally seize the Orrery, after Trazyn made use of it. The Overlord, though, would also ensure that his [[Tomb World]], [[Solemnace]], escaped the Phaeron's genocidal purge - which Akanabekh reluctantly agreed to. However while the Phaeron kept his end of the bargain, Trazyn would not do so.{{Fn|2}} 

This was after the [[Conclave of Celestial Guardians|Conclave]] gave into [[Trazyn]]'s demands to use the [[Celestial Orrery|Orrery]], after he threatened to unleash Akanabekh from the [[Tesseract Labyrinth|Labyrinth]] and the [[Necron Overlord|Overlord]]'s own [[Huntsmaster (Deathmark)|personal]] [[Deathmark]], aimed its [[Synaptic Disintegrator]] at the Conclave's leader, [[Dzukar]]. Doing so, allowed Trazyn to see the coming [[Thirteenth Black Crusade]] and its attack on [[Cadia]], as well as [[Abaddon the Despoiler]]'s efforts to create the [[Great Rift]]. This caused the Overlord to immediately leave [[Thanatos]], in order to defend Cadia and prevent the Great Rift's creation. Its not known, though, if Akanabekh still remains within Trazyn's [[Tesseract Labyrinth]].{{Fn|2}}

==Appearance==
Akanabekh is said to have a face of iron cruelty and that his body is all blades and chisel-like legs. During the [[Siege of Thanatos]], the [[Phaeron]]'s carapace had also begun to glow faintly, due to bathing in the reactor fluid of [[Oruscar Dynasty|Oruscar]]'s slain [[Necron]].{{Fn|2}}

==[[Necron Quotes#A|Quotes]]==
''"Your desires are irrelevant.  This galaxy once knelt before us, and it will do so again."''{{Fn|1}}

''"Annihilation is beautiful because it will level us. No small and great, no phaeron and subject. Living or dead. All gone. All at peace."''{{Fn|2}}

