Alactus.wikitext:
{{BloodAngelsPortal}}
'''Alactus''' was a [[Battle Brother]] of the [[Blood Angels]] in late [[M41]].{{Fn|3}}

==History==
{{spoiler|source=Blood Angels (Novel Series)}}
Alactus was a member of [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Simeon|Simeon's]] [[5th Company (Blood Angels)|5th Company]] and was over a century old as of late [[M41]].{{Fn|1a}} This placed him in an older generation than his battle-brothers [[Rafen]] and [[Arkio]].{{Fn|1c}}

Part of [[Veteran Sergeant]] [[Koris|Koris's]] [[Tactical Squad]], Alactus was deployed to [[Cybele]] along with the rest of the 5th Company. Surviving the first, devastating attack by the [[Word Bearers]], Alactus was shaken by the [[Chaos Space Marines]]' use of a [[psychic]] weapon that awakened the [[Red Thirst]] in many of his battle-brothers.{{Fn|1b}}{{Fn|1c}}

Initially cynical, Alactus was impressed by the eloquence and confidence of Brother [[Arkio]], when he rallied the dispirited Blood Angels and proposed a tactical plan that let them turn the tables on the Word Bearers.{{Fn|1c}}

Alactus was further impressed by the prodigies Arkio performed aboard the [[battle barge]] ''[[Bellus]]'' and on [[Shenlong]], handling the [[Spear of Telesto]] without effect, and spontaneously growing wings that allowed him to fly. By the end of the Shenlong campaign, the once-cynical Alactus firmly believed that Arkio was the reincarnation of the Blood Angels' [[primarch]], [[Sanguinius]].{{Fn|1d}}

===Death===
Unfortunately, Alactus's allegiance to Arkio brought him into confrontation with his former brother Rafen, who tried to escape the ''Bellus'' to the surface of [[Sabien]], after becoming convinced that Arkio had been tainted by [[Chaos]]. Rafen tried to enter the launch bay of the ''Bellus'' unnoticed, but Alactus recognized and tried to stop him, forcing Rafen to kill him.{{Fn|2}}

