Alves Scorn.wikitext:
{{QuoteBox
|quote = '''''"I do not doubt my [[Emperor]]'s wisdom in creating a necessary evil such as [[World Eaters|these fearful warriors]], nor do I doubt their effectiveness in battle. It remains my fervent hope however, that though I spend my life making war for the liberation of [[Mankind]] that I never again see such inhuman butchery as I have witnessed in the halls of [[Cerberus (Asteroid)|Cerberus]]."'''<br>- [[Colonel|Bashar-Colonel]] '''Alves Scorn''', on the [[World Eaters|XIIth Legion Astartes]], in the aftermath of the [[Cerberus Insurrection]].'''''{{Fn|1}}
|}}
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''Alves Scorn''' was an officer of the [[Imperial Army]] active in the early [[Great Crusade]] era.{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
By the later stages of the [[Unification Wars]] and the start of the [[Great Crusade]], Scorn was a [[Colonel|Bashar-Colonel]] of the [[XXIInd Dracos|XXII<sup>nd</sup> Dracos]] [[Regiment]].{{Fn|1}}

He and his forces fought alongside the [[World Eaters|XII<sup>th</sup> Space Marine Legion]] (then known as the "War Hounds") against the [[Cerberus Insurrection]]. Scorn's account of the battle, recorded in his memoirs, was one of the few existing first-hand accounts of the War Hounds' early campaigns - including not just their tenaciousness, but their savagery.{{Fn|1}}

After leaving active service, Scorn went on to become the [[Imperial Commander]] of [[Proximal Secundus]].{{Fn|1}}

