Amonther Numeriel.wikitext:
{{EldarPortal}}
'''Amonther Numeriel''' was an [[Eldar Pathfinder|Outcast Pathfinder]] from the [[Craftworld]] [[Iyanden]].{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
A survivor of the [[Battle for Iyanden]], he considered himself a coward for running while many of his family and friends fought and died fighting the [[Tyranids]]. Ashamed of his actions, he walked the [[path of the Outcast]] soon after and carried five of their [[Soulstone]]s with him at all times.{{Fn|1}}

In order to redeem himself, he aided the [[Ranger]] [[Illic Nightspear]] in his failed assassination attempt on the [[Necron Overlord]] [[Anrakyr the Traveller]] during the [[Carnac Campaign]]. After the attempt, the [[Necron]] hunted the group and Numeriel began to flee to the [[webway gate]] on [[Carnac]] that led to the safety of the [[Craftworld]] [[Alaitoc]]. He had almost reached the webway, when he was surrounded by [[Deathmark]]s. Lamenting that he had failed once again, Numeriel was killed by the Necrons.{{Fn|1}}

