Anahk'hir.wikitext:
{{NurglePortal}}
'''Anahk'hir''' is a [[Daemon Prince]] of [[Nurgle]].{{Fn|1}}


==History==
He was once summoned to the planet [[Sturmhex Prime]] by [[First Captain]] [[Roga]] of the [[Lords of Decay]].  Once there, he sought to use the dying star [[Sturmhex]] to open a [[Warp Rift]] that could form a bridgehead for one of [[Ezekyle Abaddon|Abaddon the Despoiler's]] [[Black Crusade]]s.  He was opposed by the entire [[1st Brotherhood (Grey Knights)|First Brotherhood]] of the [[Grey Knights]] [[Chapter]], who had travelled to Sturmhex Prime after receiving a warning from their [[Prognosticar]]s.{{Fn|1}}

Initially, Anahk'hir saw this as an opportunity to exact revenge on the one who banished him back to the [[Warp]].  However, the [[Sturmhex Incident|resulting battle]] went badly for the [[Daemon]] and his allies and, to add insult to injury, the individual who banished him previously was not present.  Nonetheless, Anahk'hir engaged in a duel with the Brotherhood's Grand Master, [[Vardan Kai]], in an attempt to turn the tide of the battle.  Over the course of the duel, Kai attempted to banish the Daemon by invoking Anahk'hir's [[true name]], but was unsuccessful as he had been supplied with false information by [[Inquisitor]] [[Nicodaemus Quixos]].{{Fn|1}}

However, Anahk'hir was then attacked by a squadron of [[Stormraven Gunship]]s, distracting the Daemon Prince, who took to the air to try and bring them down.  In the end, the [[Grey Knights Techmarine]] [[Aegir (Grey Knights)|Aegir]] was able to grievously wound Anahk'hir by ramming him with his Stormraven, ''[[Kodachi]]'', allowing Grand Master Kai to imprison the Daemon within a [[tesseract labyrinth]].  Following Anahk'hir's defeat, the Lords of Decay and their daemonic allies were swiftly defeated and the tesseract was presented to the Inquisitor.{{Fn|1}}

==Wargear==
*Anahk'hir was armed with a [[plague cannon]] and possessed a pair of wings.{{Fn|1}}

==Notes==
*At one point, Vardan Kai [[True name|names]] Anahk'hir as '''Anahk'hir Terrigassimal Yarnick'''.  However, it was revealed that this was not Anahk'hir's true name.{{Fn|1}}  Whether it has any other relation to the Daemon Prince is unknown.

