Andechs.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
[[General]] '''Andechs''' was a [[nobleman]] and an officer of the [[Astra Militarum]] from [[Armageddon]]. By the time of the [[Second War for Armageddon]], he had command of all [[Armageddon Steel Legion]] forces on the planet.{{Fn|1a}}

==Biography==
In the opinion of [[Commissar]] [[Sebastian Yarrick]], Andechs was a competent officer. However, Yarrick believed that Andechs's position owed more to his political abilities rather than his military record - in particular the fact that his family had connections with [[Planetary Governor|Overlord]] [[Herman von Strab|von Strab]] and his dynasty.{{Fn|1a}}

[[Second War for Armageddon|When Armageddon was invaded]] by an [[Ork]] horde, von Strab ordered Armageddon's military forces to assume a defensive deployment rather than taking the fight to the invading [[xenos]].{{Fn|1a}} Despite the views of a number of Armageddon's defenders, many of whom believed that this defensive strategy was a mistake, Andechs was unwilling to countermand his superior.{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}}{{Fn|1c}}

Later in the war, [[Colonel]] [[Artura Brenken|Brenken]], a number of [[Kanturek|other Steel]] [[Vollbrecht|Legion officers]], and [[Canoness]] [[Setheno]] confronted Andechs in his headquarters and urged him to commit forces in support of the [[Legio Metalica]]{{Fn|1c}}, which had been ordered to confront the Ork advance alone.{{Fn|1b}} Andechs refused, and so Brenken, acting with Yarrick's authority as a Commissar, executed Andechs and assumed command of the Steel Legions.{{Fn|1c}}

==Sources==
