Anders Mir.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Anders Mir''' was a [[Corporal]] of the [[Cadian 217th]] [[Imperial Guard Regiment|regiment]].{{Fn|1a}}

==Biography==
A trueborn [[Cadian]], Mir had a reputation among the 217th as an excellent [[sharpshooter]].{{Fn|1a}} He had even managed the feat of killing a [[Heretic Astartes]] on [[Zephys]] by landing a shot through its eye lens.{{Fn|1c}} However, he was also notable for his outspoken dislike for the regiment's [[transplant]]s - those non-Cadian born Guardsmen transferred from other regiments to bolster the 217th's numbers.{{Fn|1a}}

At one point in the [[Indomitus Crusade]], the Cadian 217th were deployed to fight against [[heretic]]s on the planet [[Cocleratum]].{{Fn|1a}} However, after [[Imperial]] forces were driven back from the capital city of [[Elborescum]] by the heretics, a new strategy was put forward: a team of three specially selected Cadian [[Imperial Guard Sniper|snipers]] (Mir, along with [[Sergeant (Imperial Guard)|First Sergeant]] [[Ilya]] and Corporal [[Darya Nevic|Nevic]]) would infiltrate Elborescum ahead of the main attack and assassinate the heretics' leader, [[Speccius]].{{Fn|1b}}

During the infiltration, the Guardsmen were discovered and had to flee through the '''Gardens of the Fountains'''. There, they encountered a [[Heretic Astartes]], who attacked them. He easily overpowered Mir, batting aside his [[long-las]] and throttling him. However, as the Traitor Astartes taunted the Guardsman in his grasp, Mir set off one of the [[Krak grenade|krak charges]] on his belt.{{Fn|1d}} Mir was incinerated in the blast{{Fn|1d}} but, although it was injured, the Astartes survived.{{Fn|1e}}

