==History==
The [[Warpcoven]] attacked '''Mausoleum City Fifteen''', where they became notorious for burning shrines to the ground and causing mutations to rise from the corrupted rubble. They also slaughtered with impunity the [[Ecclesiarchy]] forces that tried to stop them. Unbeknownst to the [[Imperium]], however, Daast's Warpcoven was targeting specific shrines in order to complete a pattern within the city. This only became apparent too late, after the 9th shrine fell and a perfect circle was formed. From its center a [[Warp Rift]] appeared and hundreds of [[Daemons]] poured out of it to attack Mausoleum City Fifteen. In the end, entire [[Regiments]] of the [[Astra Militarum]] were required to put down the [[Daemons]] and the Rift was closed by the [[Vipers Penitent]]'s [[Librarians]]. Daast was also one of the [[Thousand Sons]]' [[Sorcerer]]s, that [[Interrogator]]-[[Lieutenant (Imperial Guard)|Lieutenant]] [[Idon Throom]] gathered information on, while he was on [[Harlecrypt Tertius]].{{Fn|1}}

