Antonus Antwark.wikitext:
{{WordBearersPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was the [[human]] [[shipmaster]] of the ''[[Infidus Imperator]]'', the flagship of the [[Word Bearers]] [[Legion]] during the [[Battle of the Macragge's Honour]]. His immediate superior was [[First Captain]] [[Kor Phaeron]], and his opposite number was the shipmaster of the [[Ultramarines]]' flagship, the ''[[Macragge's Honour]]'', [[Ouon Hommed]].{{Fn|1a}}

==History==
[[Image:Antonus_Antwark.jpg|thumb|right|250px|{{PAGENAME}}{{Fn|1}}]]
When Kor Phaeron failed to hold the weapons platforms in [[Calth]] orbit, he and his forces escaped to the ''Infidus Imperator'', which fled the [[Veridian system]] with the ''Macragge's Honour'' in pursuit.

After the initial clash in [[realspace]] between the ''Imperator'' and the ''Honour'', Kor Phaeron decreed it was time for the ship to escape into the [[warp]]. Antwark objected that that was not possible before the [[Navigator]]s calculated a safe transit point, but Kor Phaeron simply slit the air with his ''[[athame]]'', opening a warp rift that swallowed the ''Imperator''. To the Word Bearers' surprise, the ''Honour'' followed them in.{{Fn|1b}}

Antwark noted the damage to the pursuers' engines, and guessed that the ''Imperator'' could outrun them, but Kor Phaeron ordered that the ''Imperator'' would run only long enough to break visual contact with the ''Honour'', then turn about and destroy her.{{Fn|1c}}

However, during the final attack pass, the ''Honour'' acquired a firing solution and loosed a devastating volley at the smaller ''Imperator''. Antwark reported the catastrophic damage to the ship with alarm, and turned to Kor Phaeron for orders, only to see that Phaeron had cut another hole in the air with his ''athame'' and escaped the ship. A few minutes later, the Ultramarines' second volley completely destroyed the ''Imperator'', killing Antwark and all remaining hands aboard.{{Fn|1d}}

