Aphkar.wikitext:
{{DarkAngelsPortal}}
{{QuoteBox
|quote = "'''''He who was ancient and yet ungraven by time. Whose trust grew but slowly, yet whose fealty was ironclad. Who struck true despite the tempest and the shadow.'''''"{{Fn|2a}}
|}}
'''Aphkar''' is a [[Fallen Angel]], who is among those who now loyally serve their returned [[Primarch]], [[Lion El'Jonson]]{{Fn|1c}} as the [[Risen (The Fallen)|Risen]].{{Fn|1d}}
==History==
He is a [[Terran]] '''Gyptian''', who was one of the earliest members of the [[First Legion]], Aphkar held the rank of [[Space Marine Sergeant|Knight-Sergeant]], when [[Caliban]]'s civil war began. As his vengeful [[Primarch]], [[Lion El'Jonson]], attacked their [[Adeptus Astartes Homeworld]], Aphkar and the other [[Dark Angels]] that served under [[Luther]] fought to defend themselves against their invading brethren. He personally saw the Primarch slaughtering First Legion veterans and [[Neophytes]] alike, before Caliban was [[Destruction of Caliban|destroyed]] and Aphkar was cast into the [[Warp]]{{Fn|1b}}. The Sergeant emerged into [[Realspace]] millennia later and eventually met with his fellow Fallen, [[Kai (Fallen Angel)|Kai]] and the two later met [[Lohoc]]. The three then banded together to survive in this new [[Imperium]], where the Fallen were hunted by the Dark Angels [[Chapter]] and the [[Unforgiven]]{{Fn|1c}}. Sometime after the [[Great Rift]]'s creation, they used a landing craft to travel to the [[Imperial]] world [[Avalus]] and crashed into its capital '''Xerxe'''. The three survived the crash and hid themselves shortly afterwards. They then began discreetly leaving symbols that were only understood by the Fallen and which pointed to the building they hid themselves in.{{Fn|1b}} 

They later began hearing that their [[Primarch]], [[Lion El'Jonson]], had returned to the [[Imperium]] and was now in '''Xerxe'''. This was soon proven true, when the [[Fallen]] [[Zabriel]] found their hideout and Aphkar was shocked to see him. The [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] had trained Zabriel when he joined the [[First Legion]], but now the once younger man, was vastly older than Aphkar. This was due to Zabriel being in [[Realspace]] for some four hundred years, which caused Aphkar to wince, as the Sergeant had only emerged thirty years ago. Zabriel then stated that he had been sent by the Primarch to find and recruit the Fallen{{Fn|1b}}, that El'Jonson believed resided in the Capital{{Fn|1a}}. The Primarch wished for them to fight by his side to defend the embattled [[Imperium]] and was willingly to put their differences behind them. This came about after El'Jonson met Zabriel and then learned that some of the Fallen honestly believed he had attacked them first, during the civil war on Caliban. After hearing this, Aphkar and [[Kai (Fallen Angel)|Kai]] were against aiding their Primarch, as they thought El'Jonson was responsible for the civil war and the deaths of their brethren. However both were surprised when [[Lohoc]] agreed to serve his Primarch, without a second thought, as he had never believed El'Jonson had been responsible for the civil war. Kai then agreed to meet with their Primarch, which led Aphkar to reluctantly agree to join them{{Fn|1b}}. The meeting began poorly, however, as the Sergeant still held lots of anger towards their Primarch. However after hearing El'Jonson's plea and having the Primarch promise to extend the same offer to any Fallen, who had not embraced the powers of [[Chaos]], Aphkar agreed to serve by his side. Both Kai and Lohoc agreed to do so as well.{{Fn|1c}}

