Apollyon (Inquisitor).wikitext:
{{QuoteBox
|quote = "He who allows [[Xenos|the alien]] to live shares its crime of existence."
|source = - Inquisitor Apollyon{{Fn|1a}}
|}}

{{InquisitionPortal}}
'''Apollyon''' was an [[Inquisitor]].{{Fn|1}}{{Fn|2}}{{Fn|3}}

==History==
When the planet [[Khattar]] fell to [[Chaos|heresy]] and [[Khattarn Insurrection|tried to secede]] from the [[Imperium]], Apollyon found out about this treachery and initiated a campaign to break the rebellion. The Inquisitor successfully blockaded Khattar's orbit with an [[Imperial Navy]] fleet but lacked the ground forces necessary to take the planet's surface.{{Fn|1}}{{Fn|2}} He called upon the [[Celestial Lions]] for aid, who mobilised five [[Space Marine Company|companies]] led by [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Saul (Celestial Lions)|Saul]].{{Fn|2}}

The [[Space Marines]] deployed to the surface and swiftly brought an end to the rebellion. As they prepared to depart Khattar and return to [[Elysium IX|their]] [[Adeptus Astartes Homeworld|homeworld]], however, Apollyon ordered his fleet to bombard Khattar and exterminate all [[human]] life from it, claiming that he had judged the planet's heresy as rooted too deeply to save it.{{Fn|1}}{{Fn|2}}

The Celestial Lions, appalled at the Inquisitor's actions, denounced him. They sent messages to local Imperial governments and even tried to bring word of the massacre to [[Terra]] itself. This would have dire consequences for the [[Chapter]], as the [[Inquisition]] does not suffer challenges to its authority gladly.{{Fn|1}}{{Fn|2}}

