Aqhet Hakoris.wikitext:
{{ThousandSonsPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was a member of the [[Thousand Sons]] during the [[Great Crusade]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
As a [[Space Marine Sergeant|sergeant]] in the past, he was cured of the [[Flesh Change]] with the help of [[Magnus]] himself; upon Magnus's refusal to admit how, he began to delve into the [[Warp]] himself to understand the powers of it. Hakoris would also come to believe that the Warp had [[Daemon|sentient beings]] within it, with whom one could communicate and make deals. Hakoris became [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] of the [[Ninth Fellowship]]'s Amenta-Ninety-Nine [[Space Marine Company|Circle]].{{Fn|1}}

Soon established as a powerful [[psyker]], Hakoris and his cabal of the [[Aquilae]] secretly dabbled in astral projection into the [[Warp]] in order to gleam the truth. Hakoris would later come into contact with a [[Daemon]] named [[Choronzon]]. During a symposium about recognising the legitimacy of the Aquilae as a Sixth Cult of Prospero and Hakoris as its [[Magister Templi]], Hakoris lied about this experience to Magnus - although the [[Primarch|primarch]] saw through this lie due to his psychic powers. Magnus admitted to Hakoris in private that his knowledge to cure the Flesh Change came from such daemons, although none of his sons or even the [[Emperor]] had known due to Magnus lying.{{Fn|1}}

The primarch thus encouraged Hakoris to continue the lie that he had not spoken with daemons for the remainder of the hearing. However, Hakoris ended up testifying on their existence throughout the Warp. This testimony doomed him and the Aquilae at the hearing, during which Magnus disbanded the unrecognized cult and scattered its members throughout the Legion. Hakoris was stripped of his rank and honours and doomed to eternal service as a Line Brother, but was ready to still prove his findings on the Warp.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[The Sixth Cult of the Denied (Short Story)]] — [[Blood of the Emperor (Anthology)]]

