Aradryan.wikitext:
{{EldarPortal}}
[[Image:OutcastRanger.jpg|thumb|right|250px|{{PAGENAME}} as an [[Eldar Ranger]]{{Fn|1k}}]]
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is a [[Ranger]] of [[Craftworld]] [[Alaitoc]].{{fn|1}}

==History==
While walking the [[Path of the Dreamer]] with his dream-partner [[Korlandril]], {{PAGENAME}} became distressed after witnessing dead Eldar returning from battle having their [[Spirit Stone]]s intergrated with Alaitoc's [[Infinity Circuit]]. Overcome by claustrophobia and seeking freedom, {{PAGENAME}} became a [[Path of the Steersman|Steersman]] on a starship for twenty years.{{Fn|1a}} After returning to Alaitoc he reunited with his old friends Korlandril and [[Thirianna]], but after publicily criticizing Korlandril's new sculpture their friendship fractured. Moreover, he confessed his love for Thirianna but was rejected. These acts caused {{PAGENAME}} to walk the [[Path of the Outcast]] with the [[Biel-tan]] [[Eldar Ranger]] [[Athelennil]].{{Fn|1b}}

Embracing the free lifestyle of an outcast and learning the ways of the Ranger from Athelennil aboard the vessel ''Irdiris'', his ship recieved a distress call from the [[Exodite World]] of [[Eileniliesh]], which was under [[Ork]] attacked. Aradryan brought word back to Alaitoc of the emergency, and in the subsequent war for the planet against the Greenskins he was reunited with both Korlandril, now a [[Striking Scorpion]] and Thirianna, now a [[Farseer]].{{Fn|1c}}

Afterwards, Aradryan and his fellow Rangers traveled to a [[Harlequin]]/[[Dark Eldar]] settlement in the [[Webway]] known as [[Khai-Dazaar]]. There, they join a group of mercenaries and Dark Eldar who agreed to aid them find [[Waystone]]s on a dangerous [[Crone World]].{{Fn|1d}} Traveling to the [[Eye of Terror]] with the Dark Eldar exile [[Maensith]], the Harlequin Mediator [[Estrathain]], and the [[Solitaire]] [[Lechthennian]] to the Crone World of [[Miarisillion]], they find the Waystones of the world's damned inhabitants but come under attacks by [[Daemonette]]s.{{Fn|1e}} Despite his brush with death, Aradryan was thrilled with the danger and decides to stay with Maensith and become an [[Eldar Corsair]].{{Fn|1f}}

Eventually rising to Maensith's lover and second in command, the group were successful against their raids on [[Human]] worlds. During the raid on [[Daethronin]], {{PAGENAME}} manipulated his corsair's warband into betraying their Dark Eldar allies [[Yrithain]] and [[Khiadysis]] by luring them into a trap against the [[Human]]s.{{Fn|1f}} He was able to force the Human [[Governor]] of Daethronin into giving tribute and aid to his fleet, executing the man's son to prove his power.{{Fn|1g}}

However Aradryan's arrogance eventually got the better of him. While attacking a heavily defended Human convoy, they were lured into a trap by [[Space Marine]]s and their vessel ''Fae Taeruth'' was crippled during the attack.{{Fn|1h}} Moreover, his actions against Khiadysis  caused them to seek revenge by provoking an [[Siege of Alaitoc|Imperial Invasion]] of Alaitoc. During the subsequent battle, Aradryan was able to arrive in the later stages and reveal the truth to the Imperial Space Marines, which subsequently withdrew.{{Fn|1i}} After the truth of the affair came to light, Aradryan was summoned by Alaitoic's [[Seer Council]] but was confronted by Thirianna, who revealed she had been subtlely manipulating him the entire time to avoid Alaitoc's destruction.{{Fn|1j}}

