Arbras Haax.wikitext:
{{SonsOfHorusPortal}}
'''Arbras Haax''' was a [[Sons of Horus]] [[Justaerin]] [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]], during the [[Horus Heresy]] and also served as [[Warmaster]] [[Horus]]' emissary to the [[Death Guard]].{{Fn|1b}}
==History==
This occurred in 13.[[M31]], when the [[Primarch]] [[Mortarion]] and the bulk of the [[Death Guard]] became unaccounted for, after entering the [[Warp]] to take part in the [[Solar War]]. In response, Haax was sent to the [[Traitor Legion]]'s [[Homeworld]], [[Barbarus]], to investigate their absence. The [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] was accompanied by an elite contingent of the [[Sons of Horus]] and upon his arrival, Haax finds the world's garrison to be heavily engaged in a bloody campaign of enforced conscription. When questioned by the [[Justaerin]] Captain, however, the Death Guard can not ascertain Mortarion or their Legion's fate{{Fn|1b}}. [[Vrokhorn]]{{Fn|1a}} and the garrison's other commanding officers are also not forthcoming, as to why they are in such a heightened state of activity. Though he did not discover any answers, Haax was forced to remain upon Barbarus as a conduit for the [[Warmaster]]'s will. The Captain was also ordered to bring harsh censure upon the Death Guard, should they be foolish enough to defy the will of the Warmaster as he stood on the [[Siege of Terra|threshold of victory]]{{Fn|1b}}. This would lead Haax and his forces to take part in defending Barbarus, when the [[Dark Angels]] led a [[Loyalist]] [[Siege of Barbarus|invasion]] of the world.{{Fn|1c}}

The [[Loyalists]] would subsequently [[Siege of Barbarus|conquer]] [[Barbarus]] and the [[Traitor]]s defending it were killed.{{Fn|2}}
==Canon Conflict==
[[White Dwarf 478]] states that ''Arbras Haax'' is the [[Sons of Horus]]' emissary to [[Barbarus]]{{Fn|1b}}. However [[White Dwarf 481]] states that [[Volkus Goraddin]] holds that position.{{Fn|2}} 

