Archeus.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''Archeus''' is an esteemed [[Imperial]] [[Lexicanum Loremaster]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
He conducted an expedition to study the repair subroutines of the [[Adeptus Mechanicus]] and recived an [[augmetic]] arm and heart to showcase their work. However Archeus' voicebox was also removed and he was left speaking [[binharic]], until his request for a [[Vox|Vox-Synthesiser]] was approved. Furthermore the Adeptus Mechanicus had cut up the [[Lexicanum Loremaster|Loremaster]]'s brain and then stored the parts in separate areas around his body, because of redundancy they claimed. This has caused Archeus to occasionally refer to himself in the third person when he talks.{{Fn|1}} 

On his journey back from the [[Adeptus Mechanicus]], Archeus would then encounter the [[Aeldari]]'s [[Harlequin]] faction and was among the few outside of their species to witness a dance performance by them. Though he has been forbidden by the [[Inquisition]] from speaking on how this came about, Archeus was permitted to give a lecture of the encounter to a group [[Lexicanum Loremaster|Loremaster-initiates]] - albeit one that has been redacted in parts by the Holy Ordos. His [[binharic]] lecture was transcribed by an aide and in it, Archeus described how poorly done he thought the Harlequin's performance was. Overall, the Loremaster thought the Xenos could stand to learn from the wisdom and culture of [[humanity]] in order to better improve their dances. Once he was finished speaking, Archeus accepted an invitation to present his lectures in the hallowed halls of the [[Ordo Xenos]] for a short time.{{Fn|1}}

