Arkhor.wikitext:
{|align="right"
|align="right"|{{KhornePortal}}
|-
|align="right"|{{WorldEatersPortal}}
|}
'''Arkhor the Redbound''' is a [[World Eaters]] [[Chaos Lord|Warleader]].{{Fn|1b}}

==History==
His [[Butcher's Nails]] have caused Arkhor to suffer several strokes, which necessitate the right side of his face being equipped with jury-rigged [[bionic]]s in order for it to move.{{Fn|1b}}

In [[M42]], Arkhor's [[Chaos Warband|Warband]] was plaguing the [[Gremulid System]], when the newly converted [[Chaos Space Marine]] [[Ortan Leidis]] sought to join them. The former [[Angels of the Grail|Angel of the Grail]] was drawn to the thrill of battle{{Fn|1a}} and Arkhor became a mentor of sorts and opened the path for Leidis to become a worshiper of [[Khorne]].{{Fn|1d}} The Warband would then continue their attacks in the Gremulid System, as their vessel did not have a [[Warp Engine]].{{Fn|1a}} As they did so, Leidis became obsessed with learning the ways of the [[World Eaters]] and especially how he could attain his own Butcher's Nails. To his frustration, however, Arkhor told Leidis very little about the [[Traitor Legion]].{{Fn|1d}} 

This would change, though, after Arkhor's Warband captured the [[Oath of Saint Gremulus]] and then sensed the summoning sent out by the [[Daemon Primarch]] [[Angron]] on [[Kalkin's Tribune]]. Abandoning the Oath to be destroyed by the massed World Eaters fleet that greeted them there after reaching the world, Arkhor and his Warband used a shuttle to enter the Traitor Legion's flagship, the ''[[Conqueror (Ship)|Conqueror]]''.{{Fn|1b}} Like the thousands of other World Eaters who had done so, they hoped to meet with Angron, who had only recently returned to [[Realspace]] from the [[Warp]]. The Daemon Primarch would not meet with them, however, and instead the [[Chaos Lord]] [[Kossolax]] told the World Eaters that they were being gathered to take part in an attack that Angron would lead. However, the ''Conqueror'' was entering the Warp soon and so they would have no time to return to their own warships for the journey. Arkhor's Warband stayed with their shuttle within one of the ''Conqueror's'' hangar bays{{Fn|1c}}, as it journeyed to the [[Imperial]] world [[Malakbael]].{{Fn|1d}}  

However, instead of glory, Arkhor and his warband were attacked by insane World Eaters that began to attack one another as soon as Kossolax left. Arkhor was amongst those slain during the anarchy.{{Fn|1e}}

