Armand Culcis.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Armand Culcis''' was a [[Lieutenant (Imperial Guard)|Lieutenant]] of the [[Royal Volpone 50th]], active during the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
He was a 4th generation [[Royal Volpone 50th|Royal]], who was born of the middling [[Noble House|nobles]] of [[Volpone]]'s aristocracy. Despite its level in his homeworld's society, Culcis came from a strong bloodline that had a good family history.{{Fn|1}}

During the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]], the 50th were among the forces that fought the [[Blood Pact]] on [[Gnostes]]. There, some of its [[Imperial Guard Company|Companies]] were among the Militarum that [[General]] [[Voke (General)|Voke]] commanded, as he defended the city of '''Lodden'''. As the Blood Pact attacked the city, the Royals suffered causalities, including amongst their officer class. Culcis and the ill-tempered [[Imperial Guard Captain|Captain]] [[Isaac Shiller]] were eventually among the only three left and were then under the command of [[Major]] [[Vasquez Regara]]. However, when the Blood Pact advanced upon the city, Voke's tactics to fight them backfired. This led his overextended battle line to be overrun and the General gave the order for the Imperials to retreat. Culcis and the 50th then joined the other surviving [[Guardsmen]] as they tried to escape before the Blood Pact overwhelmed them. Even then, Major Regara still ensured to instil decorum into his officers. When Culcis used the slur '''Deg''' to refer to the [[Mil-serve]] servant [[Darian (Volpone)|Darian]], Regara quickly confronted him. The Major then told Culcis to call their servants by their title or name. While the Major had to deal with such ignorant behaviour from Captain Shiller, he did not want to deal with the Lieutenant acting the same way. Culcis contritely accepted this, as they continued to retreat.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
