{{IronHandsPortal}}
'''Arnok Kraan''' of [[Clan Garrsak]] is a legendary [[Iron Father]] of the [[Iron Hands]].{{Fn|1}}

Arnok Kraan was a veteran of the [[Horus Heresy]] which saw the Iron Hands nearly destroyed. While some within the [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]] called for retribution, Iron Father Kraan clung to logic and instead he convened the council known as [[The Tempering]]. Kraan refused to join the debate and refused to influence its outcome. None can even be certain he agreed with the Tempering's outcome, for he was struck down by a mysterious assassin at its conclusion. The assassin's identity and motive are unknown, and today it is claimed that Kraan may have arranged his own death. However, rather than react with rage, Kraan's fellow Iron Fathers instead saw his logic and cold dispassion as an example to follow. His legacy lives on in Clan Garrsak, which strives to emulate dispassion.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Codex Supplement: Iron Hands (8th Edition)]], pg. 13

