Arrian Vespaysian Macrina Porphyrius.wikitext:
{{AdeptusCustodesPortal}}
'''Arrian Vespaysian Macrina Porphyrius''' is a member of the [[Adeptus Custodes]]' [[Shadowkeepers]], whose deeds in the [[Shield Host]] run as long as his [[Guardian Spear]], [[Praeses]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
[[Image:ArrianArt.jpg|thumb|right|150px|Arrian Vespaysian Macrina Porphyrius{{Fn|1}}]]
He originally petitioned the [[Shadowkeepers]]' [[Lockwarden]] commander, for a thousand days in order to join the [[Shield Host]]. As he did so, Porphyrius listed the reasons why he should be accepted. Among them were his victories, including winning the [[Blood Games]], as well as his patience and Porphyrius' resolve in the face of hardships. However the Lockwarden's attention was finally caught, when Porphyrius mentioned the lessons he learned from being in the presence of beings and artefacts so evil, that their freedom cannot be tolerated.{{Fn|1}}  

This led Porphyrius to be allowed to undergo the dozens of trials needed to be able to join the [[Shadowkeepers]]. His prior experiences greatly aided him, as some would require Porphyrius to encounter [[Daemon]]s, the [[Shield Host]] kept imprisoned within its [[Dark Cells]]. Among his trials, was staring into the nine eyes of the [[Souldelver]] for a day and a night, without blinking. Another was besting the [[Eight of the Skull]], without his [[Guardian Spear]] or [[power armor]], and breathing in the fumes of the [[Sevenfold Trimiasma]] for three hours, without seeking aid. Porphyrius also had to be able to walk away unmoved from the [[Granter of All Six Wishes]], after listening to the Daemon for an entire day. He would successfully pass all of them and went on to serve the Shadowkeepers for 183 years.{{Fn|1}} 

During that time, Porphyrius stood watch over the [[Dark Cells]] and became a noted member, whose patience and vigilance was admired by many within the [[Shield Host]]. He would leave them only once in his career, when Porphyrius captured the [[Sorrow of Karakalla]] and brought it to be imprisoned by the [[Shadowkeepers]]. However this all changed, when the [[Great Rift]]'s creation led to the [[Age of the Dark Imperium]]. In this new era, the [[Shield Host]] found itself leaving [[Terra]] more often and Porphyrius was among them that did so. This included searching for the [[Chalice of Darkalabaster]], which was stolen from the [[Dark Cells]], during the [[Battle of Lion's Gate]]. Porphyrius' hunt for the artefact led him to the [[Maelstrom]], where he discovered the Chalice was in the possession of the [[Astral Claws]] [[Chaos Warband|Warband]]. The Shadowkeeper attacked the [[Chaos Space Marines]] who held it, in order to reclaim the Chalice, but the [[Chaos Space Marines]] later plunged into the heart of the Great Rift to escape from him. Porphyrius would not let this stop him from his duty, however, and he plunged in after them. However the Shadowkeepers have not had contact with him since and they now believe Porphyrius has died in his hunt for the Chalice.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Codex: Adeptus Custodes (9th Edition)]], pg. 26 — ''Shadowkeepers: Deeds of Legends''
{{DEFAULTSORT:Porphyrius, Arrian Vespaysian Macrina}}
[[Category:Characters (Adeptus Custodes)]]

Arrian Zorzi.wikitext:
{{WorldEatersPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is an [[Apothecary]] of the [[World Eaters]].

During the [[Siege of Terra]], Zorzi went into the forest to pray and when he returned he spontaneously murdered his [[Battle-Brother]]s and took their skulls. Zorzi was subsequently exiled from the Legion, and killed even more of his Battle-Brothers. Thanks to what he calls "old faith" in himself, Zorzi claims he has overcome the insanity of the [[Butcher's Nails]]. However, he still hears the mocking voices of those he slew.{{Fn|1a}}

Arrian eventually joined the [[Consortium]] of [[Fabius Bile]] and rose to become his [[Equerry]]. Arrian accompanied Bile and [[Oleander Koh]] during their organization of [[The Shattering]] of [[M34]].{{Fn|1}} He continued to work for Bile during the journey to [[Solemnace]] to recover the lost [[Gene-Seed]] tithe. Staying aboard the ''[[Vesalius]]'' as Bile and his troops traveled to the surface, Zorzi and [[Igori]] were forced to contend with the treachery of [[Flavius Alkenex]] and his warband of Emperor's Children. During a confrontation against Alkenex and his men aboard the bridge of the ''Vesalius'', Zorzi finally let the Butcher's Nails overcome him and in a frenzy massacred most of the Emperor's Children. However he was badly wounded by Alkenex, but managed to survive thanks to the intervention of Bile's clone of [[Fulgrim]].{{Fn|1b}}

During the [[Battle of Belial IV]], Zorzi volunteered to stay behind with a force of [[New Men]] and [[Mutant]]s and hold off [[Dark Eldar]] forces, expressing his honor in serving with Fabius for as long as he did. Shortly after he was mortally wounded by the [[Tower of Flesh]] and killed by a swarm of [[Grotesque]]s.{{Fn|2}}

